ripple-figures.json: ripple's hand-built figure catalog (the figure widget's `figure`
ids), as {id: {title, params: [{key, min, max}], anchors}}: each figure's title, its
slider keys and ranges, and its anchor names in catalog order. Generated from
qbtrix/ripple-iui main at 1796fc9 (#248; packages/svelte/src/lib/figures: index.ts
for the ids, each <id>/index.ts `meta` for title, params and anchors; 7 figures, 92
anchors). Only names and ranges are vendored: geometry and drawing code stay in ripple.

card_spec holds a ripple card's figure to these ids, param keys and ranges, and anchors,
and the concierge prompt lists them, so refresh this file whenever the catalog changes.
The anchors are computed (anchorsOf), so the modules are imported with bun, not parsed:
  cat > /tmp/dump-figures.ts <<'TS'
  const root = process.argv[2];
  const { FIGURES } = await import(`${root}/index.ts`);
  const out: Record<string, unknown> = {};
  for (const id of Object.keys(FIGURES)) {
    const { meta } = await import(`${root}/${id}/index.ts`);
    out[id] = {
      title: meta.title,
      params: meta.params.map((p: any) => ({ key: p.key, min: p.min, max: p.max })),
      anchors: meta.anchors.map((a: any) => a.id),
    };
  }
  console.log(JSON.stringify(out, null, 2));
  TS
  bun run /tmp/dump-figures.ts <ripple>/packages/svelte/src/lib/figures \
    > ee/pocketpaw_ee/paw_bar/ripple-figures.json
then update this file and the counts in test_the_vendored_ripple_figures_parse
(tests/cloud/test_paw_bar_ripple_profile.py).
